  "facts": [
    "Ocean covers ~71% of Earth's surface (NOAA / USGS: 'about 71 percent').",
    "Open-ocean albedo ~0.06, i.e. it absorbs ~94% of incoming sunlight (NSIDC 'Thermodynamics: Albedo'; Payne 1972).",
    "Snow-covered sea ice albedo ~0.8-0.9; bare sea ice ~0.5-0.7 (NSIDC). Shown as 'absorbs 20%' for snow-covered ice (albedo 0.8).",
    "Ice-albedo feedback: more ice -> more reflection -> colder -> more ice (Budyko 1969; Sellers 1969 found a runaway to global glaciation).",
    "Earth's global mean surface temperature ~15 C (NASA/NOAA baseline ~14-15 C).",
    "Snowball Earth global mean estimated ~ -50 C (Hoffman & Schrag 2002, Terra Nova 14:129; Hoffman et al. 1998, Science 281:1342).",
    "Sturtian glaciation began ~717 million years ago (Macdonald et al. 2010, Science 327:1241); Marinoan ended ~635 Ma. VO: 'seven hundred million years ago'. 'Nearly pole to pole' hedges the slushball debate.",
    "Deglaciation by volcanic CO2 accumulating over millions of years with weathering shut down (Kirschvink 1992; Hoffman et al. 1998).",
    "Area poleward of latitude e on a sphere = 1 - sin(e); today's sea ice edge drawn at ~70 deg -> ~6% of ocean area (NSIDC: sea ice covers ~7% of the ocean on average)."
  ],
